  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-1)=-{90}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince $-{90}^{\u2218}$ does not lie inside the required domain, we add one full period of ${360}^{\u2218}$ to find an equivalent angle in the domain:\n\n$$\n-{90}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={270}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nThus, our first solution in the required domain is ${x}_{1}={270}^{\u2218}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its minimum values at\n\n$$\nx={270}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n\n$$\n\nSince the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}$ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x={270}^{\u2218}$ is the only solution.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
